# The sm7150 kernel still exposes the legacy ION allocator at /dev/ion, but
# platform policy dropped both the /dev/ion file_contexts entry and the blanket
# "allow domain ion_device:chr_file r_file_perms" that used to live in
# public/domain.te when ION was deprecated in favour of dmabuf heaps.
#
# Gralloc, the media stack, every QTI HAL and any app that maps a graphic
# buffer allocates through it, so restore the grant rather than enumerating the
# ~20 domains that hit it. ion_device is mlstrustedobject, which is what made
# the original platform rule safe for app domains.
allow domain ion_device:chr_file r_file_perms;
